*Razavi Fundamentals Microelectronics CMOS Models
*Technology CMOS 180nm
* Libreria unica (modelo DC/AC + parametros de ruido). Los .MODEL son identicos a los de
* ngspice/Razavi/razavi_cmos.lib; cambia solo la forma de declarar w, l, m en los subckt.
* Parametros de ruido (didacticos, calibrados contra sky130 y gf180mcuD, ver ngspice/Razavi/Extraccion_KF_AF.ipynb):
*   kf, af : ruido flicker del Level 1   S_id = kf * Id^af / (f * W * L * Cox^2)   [A^2/Hz]
*            (el ruido termico del canal, 4kT*(2/3)*gm, ya existe por defecto en Level 1)
*   NMOS: kf = 3e-29    PMOS: kf = 3.5e-30    af = 1 en ambos
*   Con W=1u, L=0.18u, Id~76uA la esquina 1/f queda en ~51 MHz (NMOS) y ~5.9 MHz (PMOS).
*   Para una esquina mas baja (p. ej. ~1 MHz en NMOS) basta bajar kf NMOS a ~1e-30.
*   Los kf/af NO afectan a las simulaciones DC/AC/transitorias, solo a .noise.
* Variante nch_rs / xnchr: igual que nch con rd = rs = 200 ohm (ruido termico 4kT/R de cada una).

.MODEL nch NMOS LEVEL = 1
+kp=100u vto=0.4
+gamma=0.4 lambda=0.1
+phi=0.3 tox=40e-10
+cgso = 9.548e-10 cgdo = 9.548e-10
+cj=9.81e-4 cjsw=1.19e-10
+mjsw=0 mj=0
+kf=3e-29 af=1

.MODEL pch PMOS LEVEL = 1
+kp=50u vto=-0.4
+gamma=0.4 lambda=0.1
+phi=0.3 tox=40e-10
+cgso = 9.548e-10 cgdo = 9.548e-10
+cj=9.81e-4 cjsw=1.19e-10
+mjsw=0 mj=0
+kf=3.5e-30 af=1

.MODEL nch_rs NMOS LEVEL = 1
+kp=100u vto=0.4
+gamma=0.4 lambda=0.1
+phi=0.3 tox=40e-10
+cgso = 9.548e-10 cgdo = 9.548e-10
+cj=9.81e-4 cjsw=1.19e-10
+mjsw=0 mj=0
+kf=3e-29 af=1
+rd=200 rs=200

.subckt xnch D G S B

.param l=0.18u w=2u m=1
.param wd = 0.48e-6
.param ad = 'w*wd'
.param as = 'w*wd'
.param ps = '2*w+2*wd'
.param pd = '2*w+2*wd'

M1 D G S B nch l=l w=w ad=ad as=as pd=pd ps=ps m=m
.ends

.subckt xpch D G S B

.param l=0.18u w=2u m=1
.param wd = 0.48e-6
.param ad = 'w*wd'
.param as = 'w*wd'
.param ps = '2*w+2*wd'
.param pd = '2*w+2*wd'

M1 D G S B pch l=l w=w ad=ad as=as pd=pd ps=ps m=m
.ends

.subckt xnchr D G S B

.param l=0.18u w=2u m=1
.param wd = 0.48e-6
.param ad = 'w*wd'
.param as = 'w*wd'
.param ps = '2*w+2*wd'
.param pd = '2*w+2*wd'

M1 D G S B nch_rs l=l w=w ad=ad as=as pd=pd ps=ps m=m
.ends
